    "claims_markdown": "Machine `desktop-3fevhd2-1c74096080`, actual CK3 1.21.0.3/build26785313, source a91dec5c80b8d04bec6029c0faf428966f177a99. R2 loaded fixedDES57 plus the original3-file initial_reform fixture, without RRF or DLL. Both named preset Faith/mainRite pairs have their exact3 core tenets, all authored27 ordinary doctrines (temporal_appointment present/conditional absent), food/alcohol and special8/2. The independent B0 and N1 save readers retain actual engine evidence; original R1 literal26/27 failure remains unchanged.\n\nR2 N1 physical12426028B SHA578fd88ffbabce11f0ee9d61a5e42dfda23ad098f3b45e5e3a9c4c69207f8961/FileID562949958241163 is date1066.9.17, actual actor36423/piety95715. Rite152/Faith14 is None, founder=head36423, selected actor/Rite/House/Dynasty critical DES binding keys absent. Original House174/Dynasty174, both heads36423 and full CoA1866 record are unchanged from B0. Unique tag DES02_N1_ROOT was inserted into the generated filename; it was not an exact whole-field replacement. Stock first-option popup results and global unrelated-inventory cause limits remain distinct from product results.\n\nRoot temporarily took sole GUI custody only after interrupting the previous operator; the original Game12980/RUN76586/source/CAS and deadlines were retained. None->Dynastic confirmation was never submitted. The actual no-change edit window was cancelled normally. Root incorrectly called its warning a five-year cooldown, then corrected the user update after exact stock script/GUI/localization review showed the must-change-draft warning. No five-year advance, new resource input, lock clearing or product setter was performed.\n\nRoot attempted normal Exit to Desktop with autosave visibly unchecked at13:28:14.969934Z, before hard13:28:15.762582Z but after the soft deadline. Original public RUN actually ended2/RED: original Popen waited Game exit0 at13:28:27.577321Z; process_pass=false/window_close_requested=true, timeout request at13:28:17.347483Z enumerated windows[]. Keeper thread exited; original CAS11185 completed/resources[]. The normal GUI attempt does not retroactively grant the public process or business pass. E1/E2 and the first confirmed Dynastic edit remain NOT_RUN. Runtime final publicverify and closure must be appended from actual later receipts.\n\nPrivate ordered release scripts fixed four concrete file/operation-custody errors and the raw SDK download producer format for the existing public cache adapter.28 offline positive/negative checks matched; synthetic download data did not constitute a real download. No formal tag/build/Steam publication has run. Source a91 separate DES static/linear checks passed; OfficialRunner job136284464463 actually failed after the Rite wire step had passed, so whole CI is not green. Its concrete later failed step is under independent diagnosis. Publication remains3/17; no additional Steam online operation was performed.\n\nNext bounded scene is a new public R3 loading the exact R2 N1, with a real None->Dynastic draft, complete native eligibility/price and one legal confirmation, then original+1/+2 physical saves. It reuses R2 preset facts, creates no fresh world, adds no extra qualification resources and does not replay any R2 action. R2 RED is retained.\n"
